{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-fallback-chain","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Two-stage fallback paths in write-final-report.sh and render_or_fallback in render-final-summary.sh introduce set±e boundaries, dead-code branches, and warning-count refresh ordering that can silently produce wrong output under failure.","prompt_body":"In `skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.sh`, verify that `rr` and `rr2` are reliably captured across the `set +e` / `set -e` boundaries in the Stage 1 and Stage 2 fallback blocks, and that `append_render_warning` is invoked before `compose_self_fallback` in every fallback path including the Stage 2 self-compose path. In `skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh`, audit the `render_or_fallback` function: the `allow_fallback` parameter has a non-true branch that removes `final-summary.md` and returns 1, but all callers explicitly pass `true` — the branch is dead code; assess whether the pre-publish path was intended to use a different `allow_fallback` value, and whether compose_self_fallback writing to `final-summary.md` in the pre-publish phase could interfere with the post-publish phase's re-render (both phases call `render_or_fallback true`, so a pre-publish fallback body may be overwritten by a post-publish renderer failure's second fallback, which could use stale refreshed counts). Also verify that `OUTCOME`, `MODE_STR`, and `DURATION` are set before `render_or_fallback` is called in both the pre and post phases. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"token-availability-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Three scripts each independently compute 'is token data available' with subtly different conditions; divergence can silently produce misleading $0.00 or spurious N/A across the two skills.","prompt_body":"Audit the token-availability gate across three files: `scripts/render-run-summary.sh` (`--cost-unavailable` flag, caller-driven), `skills/implement/scripts/write-final-report.sh` (`TOKEN_DATA_AVAILABLE=true` only when `sum_b != 0 || total_t != 0` AND `.claude.totals` parses via jq), and `skills/design/scripts/render-final-summary.sh` (`_cost_unavailable=true` when `sum_b == 0 && total_t == 0` after `jq_ok=true`). Determine whether these gates agree for the edge case where TOKEN JSON is valid, `.claude.totals` parses successfully, but all token counts are genuinely zero — does each script produce N/A (via `--cost-unavailable`) or `$0.00`, and is the behavior consistent and intentional? Also check whether the design script's `_cost_unavailable=true` path on `jq_ok=false` (corrupt JSON) skips `append-tool-failure.sh` entirely when `stderr_nonempty=false` and `trc=0` (leaving no Warning entry), while the implement script always sets `TOKEN_DATA_AVAILABLE=false` on jq parse failure with no analogous `stderr_nonempty` guard — flag any asymmetry that leaves one skill with silent undetected token-data loss. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-matrix-fixtures","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The outcome-matrix loop in test-write-final-report.sh references fixture variables ($impl_dir, $impl_st, $impl_do, $impl_bu) not defined within this diff, and assert_not_contains is used but may not be defined in the pre-existing harness.","prompt_body":"In `skills/implement/scripts/test-write-final-report.sh`, identify all fixture variables referenced in the `for outcome_case in ...` matrix loop — specifically `$impl_dir`, `$impl_st`, `$impl_do`, `$impl_bu` — and verify that each is defined before the loop runs, either in the pre-existing harness sections not shown in this diff or within the diff itself; if any are undefined the corresponding matrix entries would silently run against an empty or wrong tmpdir. Also check whether `assert_not_contains` is defined anywhere in the harness, since it is used in several new assertions (`assert_not_contains '- **PR**:'`, `assert_not_contains '- **Outcome**:'`) but is not defined in any visible hunk. In `skills/design/scripts/test-render-final-summary.sh`, confirm that the `RENDER_ARGS_LOG` stub's argument parser handles `--cost-unavailable` as a no-argument flag: the stub shifts by 2 when `$2` does not start with `--`, and by 1 otherwise — verify `--cost-unavailable` is consumed as a 1-shift flag and that the `grep -Fq -- '--cost-unavailable' "$TMP/render-args.log"` assertion would actually find it given the full `$*` capture format (`printf '%s\n' "$*"`). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
